<title>UK: Deutsche Finance adds 1.0 trln to zero coupon bond.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Finance adds 1.0 trln to zero coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond announced by lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell has been increased by 1.0 trillion lire to 4.0 trillion lire.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEUTSCHE FINANCE NETHERLANDS BV</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  DEUTSCHE BANK</p>
<p> AMT  *4.0 TRLN LIRE  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    20.JAN.32</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  7.0 PCT   PAY DATE</p>
<p> FULL FEES  25 bp     REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	=</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS(K) 5-50-500 SALE LIMITS US/UK/NL/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> NOTES     *ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 2.0 TRLN ON 07.JAN.97 AND</p>
<p>	     INCREASED TO 3.0 TRLN LIRE ON 13.JAN.97</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
